0:{"buildId":"A2KDDaJI2Oei_cuPJJym6","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","main",null,{"className":"blog-page","children":[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","article",null,{"className":"blog-article","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell blog-article-shell","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"className":"blog-back-link","href":"/blog","children":[["$","$L4",null,{"iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":16}]," All guides"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-tag","children":["Admissions"," · ","One Window archive"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Meaning of GPA & Its Importance While Seeking Admissions in the USA"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-article-intro","children":"What is GPA? W ithout knowing meaning of GPA, Many times! students get stuck with GPA. They can’t help but wonder what is a grade point 3 or a grade point 4 and how will this help them in securing admission in/their dream university in the USA. With this guide about “"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-article-body","children":[["$","section","The guide",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The guide"}],[["$","p","Meaning of  GPA”",{"children":"Meaning of  GPA”"}],["$","p","One Window has all the info you need to go through to understand the meaning and importance of GPA, scroll down now!",{"children":"One Window has all the info you need to go through to understand the meaning and importance of GPA, scroll down now!"}],["$","p","The meaning of",{"children":"The meaning of"}],["$","p","“",{"children":"“"}],["$","p","grade point average",{"children":"grade point average"}],["$","p","“",{"children":"“"}],["$","p","is abbreviated as GPA. In the United States, it is a common method of assessing academic achievement. It goes like this: Depending on the content of the course, each one is assigned a set amount of “units” or “credits.” Most courses in high school have the same amount of units, however, this is not the case in college. Most college courses have a three-unit load (about three hours of lecture per week and six hours of homework per semester), however, the number can range from fractions of one to more than five. GPA is calculated using an A, B, C, D, and F grading scale. Several grade points are allocated to each grade.",{"children":"is abbreviated as GPA. In the United States, it is a common method of assessing academic achievement. It goes like this: Depending on the content of the course, each one is assigned a set amount of “units” or “credits.” Most courses in high school have the same amount of units, however, this is not the case in college. Most college courses have a three-unit load (about three hours of lecture per week and six hours of homework per semester), however, the number can range from fractions of one to more than five. GPA is calculated using an A, B, C, D, and F grading scale. Several grade points are allocated to each grade."}],["$","p","An A grade is worth four points, whereas a B is worth three, a C is worth two, a D is worth one, and an F is worth none. Whether you’re working on secondary or college grades, the method is the same.",{"children":"An A grade is worth four points, whereas a B is worth three, a C is worth two, a D is worth one, and an F is worth none. Whether you’re working on secondary or college grades, the method is the same."}],["$","p","Check :",{"children":"Check :"}],["$","p","CGPA to GPA conversion table",{"children":"CGPA to GPA conversion table"}],["$","p","to convert your score now !",{"children":"to convert your score now !"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}],["$","section","How does your GPA work?",{"children":["$L5",["$L6","$L7","$L8"],"$L9"]}],"$La","$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le"]}],"$Lf"]}]}],"$L10"]}],["$L11"],"$L12"]}],"isPartial":"$@13","staleTime":"$14","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L15","isPartial":"$@16","staleTime":"$14","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L17","isPartial":"$@18","staleTime":"$14","varyParams":"$19"},{"rsc":"$L1a","isPartial":"$@1b","staleTime":"$14","varyParams":"$19"},{"rsc":"$L1c","isPartial":"$@1d","staleTime":"$14","varyParams":null}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@1e","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@1f"}
